# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Regenerable or large — see CONTRIBUTING.md, "What is and isn't committed".
# results/*.json, results/*.png and results/RESULTS.md ARE committed: they are
# the evidence. Everything below is either large, regenerable, or must never
# be published.
results/*.npz
results/*.parquet
results/*.joblib
results/cache/
results/smoke/

# The audit store is generated; the hash chain is only meaningful for the run
# that built it.
results/controlplane.db
# A ledger moved aside because it predates a schema change. 03_matrix.py's
# preflight tells an operator to rename rather than delete -- it is an
# append-only audit record -- so the renamed file needs somewhere to live that
# is not the repository (DECISIONS.md 155, 157).
results/*.db.pre-*
results/policy.db
results/**/detectors.db
results/detectors.db
results/*.db-journal

# NEVER committed: review labels can contain real personal data
# (CONTRIBUTING.md). Synthetic evaluation PII lives in evalsets/ and is marked
# synthetic in its manifest; this path is for real reviewer output only.
labels/
*.labels.jsonl

# Model and dataset caches
.cache/
hf_home/

# Demo scratch: a fresh chain per run, so the trace on screen is legible.
results/demo.db
results/demo_stream.json

# Derived eval sets are regenerable and large: build_longctx pads each prompt to
# 4-16k tokens, so hinglish-pii-200-longctx.json is ~8 MB. The manifest records
# its content hash, so its identity is committed and checkable after a rebuild
# even though the expansion is not. See DECISIONS.md 037.
evalsets/*-longctx.json

# Extraction caches: large, regenerable on a GPU, and the evidence they support
# is the validation run rather than the activations themselves.
results/cache-*.npz

# Kaggle API credentials -- account tokens, never committed
kaggle/access_token
kaggle/kaggle.json
kaggle/run_on_kaggle.ipynb

# Measured extraction: caches and the long-context eval set exceed the 10 MB
# staging limit. cache-*.npz is already covered; the padded eval set is not.
evalsets/triviaqa-longctx-600.json
results/kaggle/
results/*.npz

# A Round 1 results bundle downloaded to the repository root. results_bundle,
# results_bundle (1) and results_bundle (2) are tracked, and moved to round1/
# with the rest of Round 1; gitignore does not untrack them. This entry is for
# the later download only, which duplicates evidence already committed.
#
# It matters beyond tidiness: provenance() flags an artifact dirty from any
# untracked path, so while this sits here untracked every generated artifact
# records dirty: true. Those flags are accurate but they point at a file
# unrelated to the work that produced them.
results_bundle (3)/

# Working plans handed to the agent for a session. Not deliverables and not
# documentation: they describe what to build, and the build's record is
# DECISIONS.md plus git log. Ignored rather than committed for the same reason
# as the entry above -- provenance() flags an artifact dirty from ANY untracked
# path, so a plan file sitting here would stamp dirty: true on every number
# generated while it does.
implementation.md

# ffmpeg two-pass encoder logs, written into the working directory by a video
# encode of the demo. Regenerable, unrelated to any measurement, and ignored
# for the same reason as the two entries above: provenance() flags an artifact
# dirty from ANY untracked path, so these would stamp dirty: true on every
# number produced while they sit here.
ffmpeg2pass-*.log
ffmpeg2pass-*.log.mbtree

# Competition-era PDFs: the problem statements and the two deck exports. Kept on
# disk, out of the repository. Ignored rather than deleted for the same reason as
# the entries above -- provenance() flags an artifact dirty from ANY untracked
# path, so an untracked PDF would stamp dirty: true on every number generated
# while it sits here.
*.pdf

# Warrant records written by running the examples. Outputs, not inputs: they
# carry the git state and timestamp of whoever ran them, so committing one
# would put a stranger's provenance in this repository.
examples/*.warrant.json
*.warrant.json
# the revocation replay's certificate chain; a new chain per run (DECISIONS 178)
results/drift/*.db*
